<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Sodium acetate                                           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Sodium formate                                           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Wolfe’s mineral solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=265">265</a>)       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Resazurin                                                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;955.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components thoroughly, bring to a boil for 5-10 seconds, then, cool down under a stream of H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20 v/v). Distribute the medium into suitable culture vessels (e.g., 4.8 ml medium in Hungate tubes) under the same gas mixture and seal with butyl rubber stoppers. Autoclave. After cooling, aseptically and anaerobically add per liter the following solutions (autoclaved or *filter-sterilized):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 8% NaHCO<sub>3</sub> solution*                                  </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;30.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Rumen fluid, clarified (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266">266</a>)            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Prior to inoculation, add per liter the following solutions (autoclaved and stored under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% L-Cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O solution            </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;4.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution                           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;4.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Adjust pH 6.8-7.0, if necessary. Pressurize the inoculated vessels to 200kPa H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub>(80:20 v/v).       <br>
